  "claim_boundary": "This receipt proves that one fully hashed official SEC EDGAR daily ZIP was CRC-checked, structurally parsed, and materialized as exactly one compact Parquet row per physical CSV data row. Identity is the ZIP SHA-256 plus the one-based physical row ordinal; repeated requests are intentionally not deduplicated. The exact source observation is chained by its download-receipt SHA-256. Invalid source values are retained with a bit mask and counted, while the obfuscated IP field is deliberately omitted from the derived lake for data minimization. These are SEC.gov access-log requests, not unique people, filings, trades, customers, production usage, or demonstrated impact. Event date and time describe logged access; archive retrieval time is separate and does not establish the archive's exact historical public-release time. SEC warns that lost or damaged files and extraction limitations may leave the source logs incomplete.",
